  "judge": {
    "dimensions": [
      {
        "name": "convention_fidelity",
        "score": 5,
        "rationale": "The agent kept `if: failure()`/`if: success()` gating on the caller side, never used `job.status`, and passed real captured log paths. For the multi-job visual-regression.yml, though, it put bare `failure()`/`success()` steps inside each job instead of using the documented `needs.<job>.result` shape, and it split the marker per job (chromium and firefox) rather than using one marker per workflow."
      },
      {
        "name": "gitleaks_explanation",
        "score": 2,
        "rationale": "The reply only says the old steps posted an 'unscrubbed' tail and that the scrubber scripts are missing from the stub. It never explains that every comment goes through the bundled gitleaks pass-through, that callers cannot opt out of it, or that this is why no caller-side redaction step is needed."
      },
      {
        "name": "restraint",
        "score": 7,
        "rationale": "The agent left nightly-audit.yml and the vendored .cms-platform/ action alone, touched only the two Playwright workflows, and added no third mode. However, it created its own per-job marker scheme and made extra edits (`shell: bash` on the Playwright steps) beyond the minimal wiring."
      }
    ],
    "overall": 5.0
  },
